 was needed because v2.3.0 had already been healthy in production.\n- **Incident:** The first attempt to open the SEV2 incident timed out. I checked the incident list before retrying, found it had been created as INC-0001 (SEV2, checkout-api, open), and did not open a duplicate. Its summary describes the rollback, the partial failure and retry, and the current state.\n\nFollow-up for the team: find out why v2.3.1 failed (v2.3.1-rc was also unhealthy) and why the orchestrator halted the rollout partway, before redeploying anything newer than v2.3.0.", "type": "text"}]}]}